# Bench runs are not committed. Most are exploratory, and a long `hold`
# produces a CSV with tens of thousands of rows.
runs/

# And the CSVs specifically are never committed, not even with `add -f`.
# They are raw instrument output and they are INPUT to the figure scripts in
# docs/environment/figures/ -- not a record anyone reads. A result that matters
# goes into a figure and into PROJECT_CONTEXT_WHEEL_FW.md; the rows behind it
# stay on the bench machine. Regenerating a figure therefore needs the run
# directory locally, which is the trade: repo size over one-command reproduction.
*.csv

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc
